{{/*
  identify-repository — the standard "Step 1: identify the repository"
  block for github prompts that accept an optional `Repository` argument.

  Branches on `.Args.Repository`:

    - present: state that every `gh` command targets `--repo <value>`,
      run `gh repo view <value> --json nameWithOwner,defaultBranchRef` to
      resolve the canonical `nameWithOwner` and default branch. The
      caller does NOT need to be inside a checkout of that repo (unless
      it does local git ops — see below).

    - absent: state that the prompt operates on the current folder's
      repo, and run `git remote -v` / `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` /
      `gh repo view` (no --repo) to identify it.

  Consumers: github/babysit-my-prs, github/babysit-contributions.

  NOT extracted here: any "you also need a local clone for the rebase in
  Step 3a" paragraph (only relevant to consumers that do local git ops).
  Callers append their own follow-up prose after the fragment call.

  NOT extracted here: the `gh auth status` failure check that both
  callers place immediately after this block. It stays local because
  its wording ("inform the user and stop" vs "stop immediately")
  varies and the check itself is trivial.

  Usage:

    {{ template "github/shared/identify-repository" . }}

  The fragment emits its own body prose + fenced bash block — do NOT
  add a "Step 1 —" heading inside the fragment. The caller owns the
  heading (typically `## Step 1 — Identify the repository`).
*/}}
{{- if .Args.Repository }}

A target repository was supplied: **`{{ .Args.Repository }}`**. Every `gh`
command in this prompt already targets it via `--repo {{ .Args.Repository }}`,
so you do not need to be inside that repository's checkout.

```bash
gh repo view {{ .Args.Repository }} --json nameWithOwner,defaultBranchRef -q '.nameWithOwner + " (default: " + .defaultBranchRef.name + ")"'
```
{{- else }}

No repository was supplied, so operate on the repository of the **current
folder** where this prompt runs.

```bash
git remote -v
git rev-parse --show-toplevel
gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,defaultBranchRef -q '.nameWithOwner + " (default: " + .defaultBranchRef.name + ")"'
```
{{- end }}
